{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.FrobeniusLeptonMesonBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.FrobeniusLeptonMesonBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.frobenius_reciprocity_standard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.frobenius_reciprocity_standard","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L88-L95","doc":"Frobenius reciprocity: ⟨Res(V_λ), V_μ⟩_H₂ = ⟨V_λ, Ind(V_μ)⟩_H₃.\nThis means the branching multiplicity equals the induction multiplicity.\n\nFor V_(2,1) and V_(2): ⟨Res(V_(2,1)), V_(2)⟩ = 1\nFor V_(2,1) and V_(1,1): ⟨Res(V_(2,1)), V_(1,1)⟩ = 1 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.branching_dimension_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.branching_dimension_check","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L78-L82","doc":"Dimension check: dim V_(2,1) = sum of branching multiplicities × dim V_μ.\ndim(2,1) = 2 = 1·dim(2) + 1·dim(1,1) = 1·1 + 1·1 = 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sign_restricts_to_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sign_restricts_to_sign","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L73-L76","doc":"The sign rep (1,1,1) restricts to the sign lepton only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trivial_restricts_to_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trivial_restricts_to_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L68-L71","doc":"The trivial rep (3) restricts to the trivial lepton only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.standard_restricts_to_both_leptons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.standard_restricts_to_both_leptons","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The standard rep (2,1) restricts to BOTH lepton irreps. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge","label":"prop:frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.branchingH3H2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.branchingH3H2","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L49-L61","doc":"The branching multiplicities for H₃ ↓ H₂.\nFor each λ ⊢ 3 and μ ⊢ 2, gives the multiplicity of V_μ in\nthe restriction of V_λ to H₂.\n\nThese follow from the Pieri rule: remove one box from the Young\ndiagram of λ in all valid ways. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.two_unique_sum_of_squares","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.two_unique_sum_of_squares","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L29-L43","doc":"2 = 1² + 1² is the ONLY way to write 2 as a sum of positive\ninteger squares. This forces H₂ to have only 1-dim irreps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h4_artin_wedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h4_artin_wedderburn","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L26-L27","doc":"H₄ has dimension 4! = 24 = 1² + 3² + 2² + 3² + 1². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h3_artin_wedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h3_artin_wedderburn","kind":"theorem","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L23-L24","doc":"H₃ has dimension 3! = 6 = 1² + 2² + 1²: dims (1,2,1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h2_artin_wedderburn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.h2_artin_wedderburn","kind":"theorem","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/frobenius-lepton-meson-bridge.lean#L20-L21","doc":"H₂ has dimension 2! = 2 = 1² + 1²: two 1-dim irreps. ","signatureChunk":0}]}